Two failure shapes — handle them differently:
  (a) IMPLEMENTATION DEFECT — the failure points at something this story is responsible for
      (wrong colours, missing AC1-7 chrome, broken layout). Fix the code and re-run the gate.
  (b) SCOPE DRIFT IN REFERENCE — the failure points at UI that this story is not responsible for
      (downstream-story features, partial implementations expected from later stories). The
      reference PNG predates the current story's scope and the gate cannot pass until those
      stories ship. In this case you MUST stop and request explicit confirmation from Rasmus
